# GPU-clustered fat-tree (normal form, non-blocking fabric) -- LOCALITY model.
# 1024 GPUs = 128 servers x 8 GPUs. Tier 0 = the 8-GPU server switch: 8 GPUs on
# one low-latency (NVLink-class, 100ns) local switch, so intra-server traffic is
# a single fast local hop that never enters the datacenter fabric. Tiers 1-2 =
# the 200G fabric, NON-blocking among servers (no swept oversubscription).
# NOTE: htsim's fat-tree parser sizes the fabric to the leaf link speed, so a
# faster-than-fabric NVLink *bandwidth* tier can't be expressed here without
# inflating the fabric; this model captures locality + low intra-server latency.
# The NVLink bandwidth boost would need oversubscribed_fat_tree / multihomed.
Nodes 1024
Tiers 3
Podsize 64

Tier 0
Oversubscribed 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 8
Radix_Up 8
Downlink_Latency_ns 100
Switch_Latency_ns 0

Tier 1
Oversubscribed 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 8
Radix_Up 8
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Bundle 1

Tier 2
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 16
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Bundle 1
